  <main>
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">Discourse Graphs · engineering workflow</p>
      <h1>Agentic PR Workflow</h1>
      <p class="meta">Handoff · 2026-09-23 · Trang Doan · personal tooling, pilot stage</p>
      <p class="lede">The ticket-to-PR flow is rebuilt so the agent does the mechanical work and hands back <strong>evidence</strong>, not claims. A human still owns two moments: approving the plan, and requesting review. Everything in between is automated, and each automated step closes a specific trust gap.</p>
      <p>The ideas come from poteto's “2,500 PRs” talk and her <a href="https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack">pstack</a> plugin. For now it's all personal tooling in <code>~/.claude</code>. It gets proposed to the team after a short pilot.</p>
      <p><span class="status done">Phase 1 plumbing ✓</span><span class="status done">Phase 2 evidence ✓</span><span class="status done">Phase 3 Obsidian verify ✓</span><span class="status">Phase 4 pilot</span></p>
    </header>

    <section id="flow">
      <h2>The flow at a glance</h2>
      <div class="gates">
        <div class="gate"><b>Gate 1 · human</b><span>Approve the plan. Say “approved, ship when verified” to let the agent open the PR on its own.</span></div>
        <div class="gate"><b>Gate 2 · human</b><span>Review the PR and its evidence, record the Loom, request review.</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="diagram"><pre class="mermaid">
flowchart TD
    A["/start ENG-####&lt;br/&gt;worktree + app + prior context"] --> B["Plan together&lt;br/&gt;human-led · grilling · diagrams"]
    B --> G1{{"GATE 1 · human approves plan"}}
    G1 --> C["/checkpoint writes&lt;br/&gt;## Approved plan"]
    C --> D["Agent implements"]
    D --> V["Agent verifies at the&lt;br/&gt;lowest rung that proves it"]
    V -->|fails| D
    V --> P["/create-pr&lt;br/&gt;checks · reviews · drift check · body"]
    P -->|unplanned structure| H["Pause: ask human"]
    H --> P
    P --> O["PR opened ready, not draft"]
    O --> BS["babysit loop&lt;br/&gt;CI + Devin · Codex · Graphite"]
    BS -->|finding fixed| L["Propose lesson&lt;br/&gt;type › lint › test › helper › prose"]
    L -->|human yes / no| BS
    BS --> G2{{"GATE 2 · review, Loom, request review"}}
      </pre></div>
      <div class="callout"><strong>Why PRs open as ready, not as drafts.</strong> Codex never reviews drafts and Graphite almost never does (checked on about 60 PRs). The repo has no CODEOWNERS file, so opening a PR as ready doesn't notify anyone.</div>
    </section>

    <section id="roles">
      <h2>Who does what</h2>
      <div class="tbl"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Human</th><th>Agent</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Plan</td><td>Leads, decides, approves</td><td>Asks questions, draws diagrams, stores the approved plan</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Implement and verify</td><td>—</td><td>Writes the code, proves it works in the real app</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Review</td><td>—</td><td>Delegated fresh-context review, scope-check, standards check</td></tr>
          <tr><td>PR body</td><td>—</td><td>Fills the repo template: reviewer diagram and evidence</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bot feedback</td><td>Approves or rejects each proposed lesson</td><td>Fixes findings, waits until all three bots have reviewed the latest commit</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hand-off</td><td>Checks the evidence, records the Loom, requests review</td><td>Writes the Loom shot list from the scenario matrix</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <p>If you didn't say “ship when verified” at gate 1, the agent stops before opening the PR and shows you the body instead.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="ladder">
      <h2>Verification ladder</h2>
      <p>The agent picks the cheapest check that can actually prove the change.</p>
      <div class="diagram"><pre class="mermaid">
flowchart LR
    U["Unit tests&lt;br/&gt;vitest + obsidianStub&lt;br/&gt;logic · converters · utils"] --> R["Roam live&lt;br/&gt;playwright:load-extension"]
    U --> O["Obsidian live&lt;br/&gt;dg-obsidian-cdp-verify"]
    R --> E["pr-evidence&lt;br/&gt;screenshots → public URLs"]
    O --> E
    E --> B["PR body&lt;br/&gt;scenario matrix · screenshots&lt;br/&gt;tests · Not verified"]
      </pre></div>
      <p>The PR's Verification section always has four parts:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>a scenario matrix (input, expected, actual, pass)</li>
        <li>screenshots</li>
        <li>the tests added, with the command to rerun them</li>
        <li>an explicit <strong>Not verified</strong> list</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="obsidian">
      <h2>How Obsidian live checks work</h2>
      <p>One command drives the real Obsidian app over the Chrome DevTools Protocol, run from the worktree root:</p>
      <pre class="cmd">node ~/.claude/skills/dg-obsidian-cdp-verify/scripts/run.mjs \
  --slot 1 --marker "&lt;symbol from the change&gt;" --scenario my-scenario.mjs</pre>
      <div class="diagram"><pre class="mermaid">
sequenceDiagram
    participant A as Agent
    participant D as Doctor
    participant O as Obsidian test vault
    participant E as pr-evidence
    A->>D: which vault slot, is it free?
    D-->>A: free, or held by another run (switch slot)
    A->>O: attach on :9222, or quit and relaunch with debug port
    A->>O: build this worktree into the vault, reload plugin
    A->>O: preflight: loaded bundle contains the marker?
    loop each scenario
        A->>O: drive UI, assert, screenshot
    end
    A->>A: write scenario matrix + last-run.json
    A->>E: upload screenshots
    E-->>A: public URLs + Markdown table
      </pre></div>
      <ul class="rules">
        <li><strong>Test vaults are changed in place.</strong> They're listed in <code>apps/obsidian/.env</code> as <code>OBSIDIAN_VERIFY_VAULTS</code>, and <code>--slot</code> picks one.</li>
        <li><strong>Everything a run creates goes under <code>_verify/&lt;branch&gt;/</code>.</strong> Folders are never deleted.</li>
        <li><strong>A lock file stops two agent runs from driving the same vault.</strong></li>
        <li><strong>The agent may relaunch Obsidian itself</strong> to add the debug port.</li>
        <li><strong>The preflight marker check catches stale builds.</strong> Another worktree's dev watcher can overwrite the vault's plugin, and this check stops that from producing a false pass.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The first verified run was the ENG-2114 insert-link scenario: 3/3 passed, in about 6 seconds when attached.</p>
